<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to the definition</a>
<header>
<div class="eyebrow">Hengshi Design v1 · Founder review · 5 October 2026</div>
<h1>One company.<br>Two ways to explore it.</h1>
<p>A complete, readable company website and a visitor-entered World share the same approved information, evidence and discovery-booking journey. This board explains the intended system; it is a review document, not the production homepage.</p>
<p class="small">Accepted decisions: D-025, D-035, D-036 and later UX amendments; D-064 movement, D-065 architecture, D-066 original modular HQ, D-067 nature-integrated direction; D-068 deferred cloud planning, D-069 v1/latest compatible, D-070 Europe-first/company contacts; D-071 campus layout basis. Detailed contracts, appearance and production evidence remain proposed.</p>
<nav aria-label="Definition sections"><a href="#journey">Visitor journey</a><a href="#optional-sound">Optional sound</a><a href="#campus">Campus direction</a><a href="#departments">Departments</a><a href="#staff">Staff and consultations</a><a href="#system">System boundaries</a><a href="#publication-flow">One publication</a><a href="#engineering">How we build it</a><a href="#features">Feature definitions</a><a href="#checkpoint">Review checkpoint</a></nav>
</header>
<main id="main">
<section id="journey"><div class="eyebrow">The first visit</div><h2>The website opens first.</h2>
<ol class="flow"><li><strong>Browse the company</strong>Read services, approved evidence and how to book. No 3D or sound is required.</li><li><strong>Choose Enter World</strong>An explicit action enters the immersive journey. Selecting a graphics stream alone does not enter the canvas.</li><li><strong>Use the supported stream</strong>Automatic capability selection respects the ceiling and accessibility settings. A visitor can explicitly apply an allowed simpler selection.</li><li><strong>Explore or return</strong>Move with mouse/touch, choose destinations, read department boards and ask for help. Equivalent semantic routes remain available.</li></ol>
<div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="tag">Accepted</span><h3>Four peer streams</h3><p>Detailed 3D, Balanced 3D, Simplified 3D and Quick Access share core information and actions. Quick Access needs no WebGL.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag">Accepted scope</span><h3>Movement and streaming</h3><p>Mouse/touch free steering and walking, alongside destination navigation. Load nearby areas and retain a buffer for reversals. WASD was not selected.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Detailed mechanics proposed</span><h3>Control and comfort</h3><p>Final gestures, collision/loading limits and screens need acceptance. Sound begins off; opt-in ambience follows outdoor and department context, with persistent mute/volume.</p></article></div>
<p class="small">The mode control is also available on the initial homepage. Existing approved stream precedence and Apply behaviour remain binding; this sequence does not remove those controls or automatically select a new stream during movement.</p>
<details id="semantic-seo"><summary>How SEO works for the website and the World</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Publish one reviewed source</strong>Staff prepare services, evidence and editable company facts. Review and approval apply to that exact version. An admin edit cannot immediately change the public footer, department board or search description.</li><li><strong>Serve complete readable pages</strong>Each eligible page has its content, clean links, title, canonical address and permitted structured facts in the initial HTML. Browsing services and reaching Book do not depend on loading the 3D World.</li><li><strong>Connect the same content to 3D</strong>Department boards use the approved release and link to their corresponding semantic pages. Graphics choices and free movement change presentation, not company facts or the creation of extra indexable copies.</li><li><strong>Check the delivered result</strong>Inspect real responses with JavaScript disabled, visible facts against structured data, statuses, canonicals, sitemap exclusions and performance. Only eligible canonical indexable pages enter the active sitemap; drafts and private conversations do not.</li></ol><p class="small">This explains project-controlled SEO requirements and their current amendments; it is not a published page or working generation pipeline. Europe is the first market, not an office claim. Supplied company facts still need evidence and disclosure review; account/domain verification and search submission remain separate actions. Exact rendering/security mechanisms, the complete compatible stable graph, production references and actual response/browser evidence remain held. These cards create no new route, schema type or ranking commitment.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-foundation/03-seo-entity-route-editorial-strategy.md#current-v1-authority--reconciled-2026-10-05">Controlling SEO strategy and current amendments</a><a href="06-entity-and-public-contact.md">Editable company facts and disclosure boundaries</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#semantic-preparation-engineering-proposal">One-snapshot semantic preparation proposal</a></div></details>
<details id="optional-sound"><summary>How sound follows the visitor without taking over</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Begin in silence</strong>The website and World remain complete without sound. Optional ambience is not fetched or played before informed enablement; remembered volume cannot enable a new visit by itself.</li><li><strong>Enable the current place</strong>Nature layers belong outdoors, with quieter reception and department ambience. Only the current ready, eligible context may start prepared sound; a loaded building or camera turn cannot enable it.</li><li><strong>Keep control as you move</strong>Persistent mute and volume take priority over blends. Hidden tabs and graphics interruptions pause ambience. On return, retain preferences and resume only when the context is safe and the browser permits; otherwise offer a silent retry.</li><li><strong>Recover quietly</strong>Late downloads cannot restart muted, abandoned or withdrawn sound. Failure keeps information, help and booking usable. Real speech or consultation media retains its own consent, alternatives and controls.</li></ol><p class="small">This is a researched lifecycle proposal; independent review and integrated acceptance are separate gates. Read the controlling definition for its precise status. It adds no audio to this board or model. Exact sound assets/rights, formats, levels, transition timings and device-memory limits remain held. Browser playback permission is separate from the visitor's choice; enabling ambience does not permit microphone capture, recording or conversation storage.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-3d/WORLD_EXPERIENCE.md#audio-lifecycle-and-ownership-proposal">Controlling audio lifecycle and ownership proposal</a><a href="../phase-1-3d/WORLD_EXPERIENCE.md#sound">Sound zones and silent equivalents</a></div></details>
</section>
<section id="campus"><div class="eyebrow">Original modular headquarters</div><h2>Technology within a thriving landscape.</h2><p>A dominant central reception, five distinct organic service wings, linked terraces and gardens, a river valley and distant layered terrain. The landscape expresses a design vision of advanced living in harmony with nature.</p>
<figure><img src="../phase-1-3d/concepts/nature-campus-direction-2026-10-04.png" alt="Selected nature-integrated concept with three views: an organic reception and department campus in a river valley, its arrival walkway, and a warm department with an information board and consultation seating."><figcaption>The founder-selected concept direction. These three artistic views are reference material, not a measured floor plan, environmental certification or completed 3D asset.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="grid two"><article class="card"><h3>What carries into the build</h3><p>The founder accepts the latest model's central reception, five-wing arrangement and connected landscape as the layout basis under D-071. Reusable building, tree and terrain parts support variation; authored collision-ready areas and nearby loading remain to be built.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>What still needs proof</h3><p>Final appearance, authored collision/thresholds, realistic materials, department interactions and measured loading budgets. The latest study has three views from one export, graded terrain and visible crossings; its sampled geometry and viewer behavior have bounded independent review. Its composition is the accepted layout basis; it remains a low-detail study without safe-walking or production acceptance.</p><a href="../../artifacts/nature-campus-layout-study/index.html">Inspect the latest isolated 3D study</a><p><a href="../phase-1-3d/spatial-storyboard.html#layout-study">Review the latest layout, three views and remaining spatial gaps</a></p><p class="small">Orbit/zoom preview only. Free walking, streaming, sound and live staff are not implemented there. The Atlanta asset remains protected separately.</p></article></div>
</section>
<section id="departments"><div class="eyebrow">Five wings · ten service categories</div><h2>Each department helps a visitor decide.</h2><div class="grid two">
<article class="card"><h3>Strategy &amp; Transformation</h3><p>Strategy &amp; Architecture.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Digital Products &amp; Growth</h3><p>Platform &amp; Product Engineering; Product Design &amp; Experience Engineering; Commerce, Content &amp; Growth Platforms.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>AI, Data &amp; Automation</h3><p>AI Systems &amp; Agentic Automation; Data Platforms &amp; Analytics.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Immersive &amp; Creative</h3><p>Spatial Computing &amp; Immersive Platforms; Creative &amp; Visual Design Services.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Cloud, Reliability &amp; Trust</h3><p>Cloud, DevOps &amp; Platform Reliability; Security, Privacy &amp; Trust Engineering.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Interaction form still proposed</span><h3>Information → guidance → conversation</h3><p>Read approved information and evidence boards. Ask clearly identified AI for sourced guidance. Reach a human only when explicit current availability is verified; otherwise use approved Contact/Book.</p></article></div>
<p class="callout">Rooms reserve the service structure. They do not prove every service, expert or live staff member is ready for launch. Held content remains held; fictional examples never become client work.</p>
</section>
<section id="staff"><div class="eyebrow">How the team supports the visitor</div><h2>A consultation has a real owner.</h2><p>The department board offers approved information, AI guidance, human help and direct booking. The proposed staff console handles the work behind those choices. These diagrams explain the system; they show no live staff or functioning console.</p>
<ol class="flow"><li><strong>Staff declares availability</strong>An authorized team member explicitly turns availability on for an approved department. An expired, withdrawn or unknown setting is unavailable.</li><li><strong>Visitor chooses human help</strong>The visitor consents to the permitted context transfer. Public availability offers help; it does not reserve a person or promise a response time.</li><li><strong>Operator accepts the request</strong>The Hengshi console checks current consent, eligibility and assignment. One guarded acceptance creates one conversation owner.</li><li><strong>Continue the conversation</strong>Governed text stays in the console. Voice/video needs separate opt-in. Direct Book and verified Contact remain recovery choices.</li></ol>
<div class="grid two"><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Reconciled data proposal</span><h3>Intent and presence are different</h3><p>PostgreSQL records the authorized declaration. Redis holds its expiring presence view. A stored declaration alone cannot mean someone is online; stale signals, cache loss or revocation cannot keep the department available.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag">Accepted boundary</span><h3>Teams alerts the team</h3><p>Teams can suppress false availability and carry approved alerts. It does not create availability or own the visitor conversation. Alert delivery is separate from request acceptance and staff response.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag">Accepted workflow</span><h3>Booking has its own truth</h3><p>A visitor can book without chat or human handoff. Qualification, verified email and an eligible slot lead to a pending submission. Confirmation requires matching provider and local evidence; an alert or timeout cannot invent it.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Exact policies held</span><h3>Exceptions remain visible</h3><p>Operators inspect assignment, alert and booking exceptions within their approved scope. Pending stays pending until reconciled. Staff identities, delegates, expiry intervals and private-record retention still need their reviewed definitions.</p></article></div>
<details id="staff-availability"><summary>What happens when a team member turns live help on or off?</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Declare for an approved scope</strong>An authorized team member explicitly chooses on or off for their permitted department scope. A role label, Teams status or department selection cannot grant that power.</li><li><strong>Save the guarded intent</strong>The server checks current authority and the expected setting before saving. Stale edits require review; an uncertain save stays pending. Retrying the same action checks its outcome without repeating or renewing it.</li><li><strong>Verify a live offer separately</strong>A saved on declaration is not proof that help is live. Current intent, eligibility and fresh presence must agree before offering it. A previous receipt or a loaded room cannot reserve a person or confirm human acceptance.</li><li><strong>Withdraw and recover safely</strong>Off removes the initiating console's live claim immediately while the save is checked. Completion needs authoritative evidence that an older on cannot take effect afterward. Existing conversations and bookings keep their own state; Contact and Book remain available.</li></ol><p class="small">This explains the independently reviewed staff-declaration proposal. Exact staff/delegate grants, expiry and renewal policy, bounded transport/retries, retention and physical enforcement still need acceptance and actual tests. It is not a working staff control or a promise that every visitor's screen changes instantly. An older save response cannot overwrite a newer choice, and uncertainty cannot be shown as success.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/AVAILABILITY_WRITE_HTTP.md">Controlling staff declaration and recovery contract</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/availability-write-http-v1-2026-10-05.md">Bounded independent contract review and remaining proof</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/AVAILABILITY_READ_HTTP.md">Separate public availability read</a></div></details>
<details id="human-consultation"><summary>What happens after a visitor asks to speak with the team?</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Choose what may be shared</strong>The visitor reviews the permitted context and purpose before consenting. An earlier ephemeral chat is not silently saved. If required notices or data policies are unapproved, that request stays held; browsing, ephemeral guidance and direct Book remain options.</li><li><strong>Wait for a real acceptance</strong>The server creates one guarded request under the approved policy. Waiting is not a human response. An uncertain save checks the same action before retrying; a Teams alert cannot accept the request or create another owner.</li><li><strong>Connect with the current owner</strong>One eligible authorized operator accepts. Text connects separately, with current consent and assignment checked. Reconnecting cannot give an old operator access or recover lost ephemeral content from a hidden copy. Voice/video always needs separate visitor opt-in.</li><li><strong>End and recover truthfully</strong>An uncertain ending stays pending until checked. Ending text does not prove deletion or cancel a booking. Availability off stops new live offers under its guard; existing conversations keep their own authorized state. Contact and Book remain recovery choices.</li></ol><p class="small">This explains the independently reviewed consultation lifecycle proposal. Its bounded PASS covers the definition; integrated acceptance and actual enforcement remain separate. Named owners, queue/reassignment policy, legal consent and retention, exact messages and limits, Microsoft/media capabilities and actual concurrency/browser evidence are still required. These cards are an explanation, not a working consultation interface or a response-time promise.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/HANDOFF_LIFECYCLE.md">Controlling consultation lifecycle proposal</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/handoff-lifecycle-v1-2026-10-05.md">Bounded independent contract review and remaining proof</a><a href="../phase-1-ux-architecture/FLOWS.md">Visitor and staff journey definitions</a></div></details>
<details><summary>Who can edit, review and approve company information?</summary><p>Author → independent specialist review → founder approval → verified preparation and activation. A new edit invalidates review of the old snapshot. Administrator access does not grant publication, conversation or booking powers; one person holding several roles cannot approve their own material.</p><p>Company facts edited in admin follow the same release workflow. The website, World boards and AI use the same eligible approved content. Knowledge review verifies the exact grounding bundle and cannot replace founder approval.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/SECURITY_PRIVACY_CONTRACT.md#proposed-action-and-object-authorization">Role and object boundaries</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/INTERFACE_CATALOG.md#added-operation-traceability">Staff operation definitions</a></div></details>
<p class="callout">When current availability cannot be verified, show unavailable and retain the usable information, AI where eligible, and Contact/Book routes. No avatars, desks or presence indicators may imply a team member is waiting when the system has no verified basis.</p>
<p class="small">The availability split, additional interfaces and field/permission definitions passed the bounded independent documentation review at its listed hashes; integrated acceptance remains pending. Exact schemas, operational grants, expiry and legal retention remain held. No staff account, mailbox owner or new operational permission is assigned here.</p>
</section>
<section id="system"><div class="eyebrow">Accepted architecture boundaries</div><h2>Shared truth, separate responsibilities.</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Web application</h3><p>Semantic pages, World and staff screens. Displays approved content and server-provided states; cannot approve publication or confirm a booking itself.</p><p class="small">React · TypeScript · Vite · Tailwind · React Three Fiber / WebGL</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Modular API</h3><p>Enforces staff roles, review/publication, consent, AI routing, booking and privacy lifecycle. External writes need durable intent and verified outcomes.</p><p class="small">FastAPI · SQLAlchemy · Alembic</p></article><article class="card"><h3>PostgreSQL truth</h3><p>Durable approved state. Immutable release artifacts feed HTML, metadata, sitemap, AI knowledge and 3D panels. Redis and search remain ephemeral or rebuildable.</p><p class="small">Native local servers; Docker not required · Hosting selection deferred</p></article></div>
<details><summary>Market, company details and contact channels</summary><p>Europe is the first target market, with broader global ambition. The legal entity is HENGSHI DESIGN (SMC-PRIVATE) LIMITED in Pakistan. Targeting Europe does not imply a European office or choose a hosting region.</p><p>Company registration, validity, address and contact facts will be editable in admin as reviewed, versioned content. General contact: info@hengshidesign.com. Separate privacy@hengshidesign.com and security@hengshidesign.com aliases are approved; the founder will create them. Ownership stays undecided. Their operation and publication evidence remain unverified.</p><a href="06-entity-and-public-contact.md">Review exact company facts and disclosure boundaries</a></details>
<details><summary>Technology and deferred hosting decisions</summary><p>This is the first product development: v1. The rule is the latest mutually compatible stable set for every tool, library and framework, verified across the full coupled graph. That production set is not yet selected. Individually newest versions are observations.</p><p>Deployment, provider, region and cost planning are deferred. Azure and AWS are candidates; lowest feasible cost/free services are preferred when planning resumes. Outlook/Teams remain intended without a Microsoft 365 setup prerequisite. Each required account/API capability needs separate proof; approved staff identity and AI privacy routes remain unchanged.</p><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PROVIDER_SCOPE_ADDENDUM.md">Review provider and Microsoft integration scope</a></details>
<details><summary>What SEO covers inside this project</summary><p>Complete semantic pages before JavaScript; verified content; navigation, metadata, canonical URLs, structured data, sitemaps, redirects and crawlability/performance checks. The World presents the same approved release and connects to canonical pages.</p></details>
<details><summary>What privacy and recovery must guarantee</summary><p>No launch visitor accounts/uploads. Non-consented chat is ephemeral. Consented chat/brief/lead has the approved 90-day rule; booking, audit and other classes need their own reviewed policies. Verified deletion must survive restoration. AI uses approved evidence and approved data routes; unknown results do not become confirmations.</p></details>
<details id="publication-flow"><summary>How one publication stays consistent across the website and World</summary>
<ol class="flow"><li><strong>Review the exact content</strong>Staff prepare company facts, services and evidence. Independent review and founder approval apply to that version. An edit creates new work to review; it cannot change public pages or boards immediately.</li><li><strong>Prepare one complete release</strong>Readable pages, search metadata, approved AI knowledge and department boards come from the same approved source. Check the generated content, code and asset associations before activation. A successful render cannot publish itself.</li><li><strong>Keep the page tied to its release</strong>The page carries its release, route, planned page-artifact and client-build identities as data. Startup reads that exact eligible release and checks the associations. It cannot silently replace a stale page with parts of the newest release.</li><li><strong>Enter the matching World deliberately</strong>After Enter World and an applied supported 3D stream, use that release's scene description and matching model interpretation. Load the requested ready areas and their required resources. Listing the campus does not download every wing; sound retains its separate enablement gate.</li></ol>
<div class="callout"><strong>If something no longer matches:</strong> block the affected enhancement, stop travel before unready ground and explain retry, Exit or verified Quick Access recovery. A withdrawn release cannot authorize new content/resource use. Moving to a fresh eligible release follows the defined recovery flow; it cannot mix new boards into an old scene or automatically relax code permissions.</div>
<p class="small">A release is a checked set of content and associated artifacts, not an immediate result of an admin edit. The proposed client catalogue records the emitted code and supported model interpretation; page metadata cannot choose executable code or prove its trust. These proposals have separate bounded independent reviews. Object-shape checks do not prove actual rendering, safe embedded-data parsing, code integrity, publication/withdrawal enforcement or browser loading. Format and integrated/founder acceptance, the complete compatible stable graph, actual renderer/serving mechanisms, permissions, rights and measured limits remain held. This board illustrates the intended flow; it does not run a publication service.</p>
<div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#semantic-preparation-engineering-proposal">Prepare from one approved source</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#client-build-identity-and-registered-entry-proposal">Client catalogue and reserved entries</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#public-html-binding-proposal">Page release/build binding</a><a href="../phase-1-3d/SCENE_ASSEMBLY_CONTRACT.md#scene-lookup-and-build-agreement-proposal">Matching scene lookup</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/public-html-binding-v1-2026-10-05.md">Binding review and remaining proof</a></div>
</details>
<details id="browser-security"><summary>How we protect pages, content and World resources</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Serve the reviewed page</strong>The public page keeps its verified release bytes. The proposed browser policy admits controlled code and checks any required inline script against its reviewed hash.</li><li><strong>Keep content as data</strong>Company facts, board text and AI output cannot become executable code or choose script/decoder URLs. Public page data excludes private conversations, staff records and internal job details; embedded data needs safe HTML-context serialization.</li><li><strong>Review World permissions</strong>Model decoders may need background workers and WebAssembly. Their resources and permissions require separate proof. Enter World cannot relax the page's HTTP policy; code, campus assets and sound retain their entry and consent gates.</li><li><strong>Recover without weakening protection</strong>If policy or decoder checks fail, keep the readable website and Quick Access available. Stop before unready ground and retain retry or Exit; never automatically broaden permissions.</li></ol><p class="small">Content Security Policy (CSP) tells the browser which resources may run or load. It complements server permissions, consent and release eligibility. This proposal has bounded independent review PASS; exact resource origins, style handling, serialization and worker permissions, the complete stable graph, real build/browser enforcement and founder acceptance remain held. This review board does not implement those controls or certify application security.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/SECURITY_PRIVACY_CONTRACT.md#browser-resource-and-serialized-content-proposal">Controlling browser-resource and serialization proposal</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/browser-resource-security-v1-2026-10-05.md">Independent proposal review and remaining proof</a></div></details>
<details><summary>How publication and live availability stay trustworthy</summary><p>The proposed publication reads verify that the release is still eligible and that its identity and content match. A withdrawn release cannot be served just because its bytes remain cached. Conditional responses cannot silently substitute a different release.</p><p>A staff declaration alone does not offer live help. Current authority, the matching declaration and fresh presence must agree at the decision point. Turning availability off removes the initiating screen's live claim immediately; confirmed global withdrawal requires authoritative evidence. A live offer remains separate from a human accepting the request.</p><p class="small">These contract proposals have bounded independent review. Four schema-tooling tests pass; there is no new running publication or availability service. Exact limits, public availability fields, permissions and concurrency/recovery evidence remain required. Privacy and security email ownership stays undecided.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_READ_HTTP.md">Public release-read contract</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/publication-read-http-2026-10-04.md">Publication HTTP review</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/publication-read-error-schema-2026-10-04.md">Error-schema review and test limits</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/AVAILABILITY_CONSISTENCY.md">Availability consistency contract</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/availability-consistency-2026-10-04.md">Availability review and remaining proof</a></div></details>
</section>
<section id="engineering"><div class="eyebrow">Engineering proposal · inside the accepted architecture</div><h2>From your vision to a complete visitor journey.</h2>
<p>You provide the vision. We research the technical choices, recommend the solution, explain consequential tradeoffs and build reviewable results. The accepted reception and five-wing composition carries forward into a connected, eye-level experience with coherent surroundings in every permitted viewing direction.</p>
<div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="tag">Accepted technology family</span><h3>Render the campus</h3><p>React Three Fiber and Three.js with WebGL connect the campus to the website. Blender supplies editable building and landscape assets, exported separately for efficient delivery.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Recommended evaluation</span><h3>Walk and look safely</h3><p>Mouse/touch input drives an upright camera and a collision-aware mover. Evaluate Rapier's character controller. Clicked destinations use safe connected routes; evaluate an authored route graph before adding navigation-mesh tooling.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Engineering proposal</span><h3>Load around the visitor</h3><p>A connected-area scheduler loads current and nearby spaces and retains recent ground for turn-backs. Download, decoding, rendering resources and collision readiness are separate stages. Unready ground cannot be crossed.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Appearance work remaining</span><h3>Create a believable place</h3><p>Near ground, surrounding buildings and vegetation, distant terrain and sky form one landscape. No exposed island edge or mountain wall on visitor routes. Inspector orbit and target-centred zoom are replaced by the designed walking controls in production.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag">Accepted authority boundary</span><h3>Connect real information</h3><p>Department boards, AI guidance, current staff availability and booking use the same eligible content and authoritative API as the semantic website. A decorative person or downloaded room cannot claim live staff or a confirmed booking.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">Measured selection required</span><h3>Control cost on the device</h3><p>Spatial batches, reusable assets, detail variants and evaluated compression reduce work. Track shared resource ownership and release unused memory. Choose exact settings and libraries through compatible stable versions and actual-device measurements.</p></article></div>
<details id="spatial-loading"><summary>What happens when a visitor walks or turns back</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Keep the current ground safe</strong>The visitor's supporting ground and active doorway stay protected. Scenery outside the camera view can still be needed for movement.</li><li><strong>Prepare connected spaces</strong>Load nearby and requested areas, verify their assets and prepare matching graphics, ground and collision. A download alone never opens a doorway.</li><li><strong>Admit safe movement</strong>Enter only a complete, eligible area. Turning back changes loading priorities and retains recent ground within the measured budget. If a path is unready, stop before it and offer retry or Quick Access.</li><li><strong>Release resources carefully</strong>Unused areas release their own resources. Trees or materials shared by another ready area stay available. Late cancelled work cannot restore movement; graphics failure stops travel and keeps accessible recovery.</li></ol><p class="small">The loading definition has bounded independent review PASS after one graph-policy clarification. This explains intended behavior; the model viewer still has no walking or streaming implementation. Exact device limits and runtime evidence remain required.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-3d/CAMPUS_ASSET_BUILD_SPEC.md#loading-and-residency-contract">Controlling loading and residency definition</a><a href="../phase-1-3d/reviews/campus-loading-contract-v1-2026-10-05.md#correction-1-verification--superseding-bounded-verdict">Independent loading review and remaining proof</a></div></details>
<details id="semantic-preparation"><summary>How the searchable website and World stay in step</summary><ol class="flow"><li><strong>Approve one content snapshot</strong>Reviewed services, evidence, company facts and eligible routes supply the public content. Private staff, conversation and booking records are excluded.</li><li><strong>Prepare the complete pages</strong>The proposed build process creates readable HTML, matching interactive-page data and the release's sitemap, knowledge and department panels. The initial website works without loading the campus.</li><li><strong>Verify before activation</strong>Build jobs return staged outputs or a failure. The publication coordinator independently checks the exact input, output bytes and required dependencies. A delayed, conflicting or partial result cannot activate itself or replace a newer attempt.</li><li><strong>Keep visits coherent</strong>Page navigation, World panels and AI remain bound to eligible release content. Live staff availability and booking use separate current API evidence; stored page content cannot invent a live status.</li></ol><p class="small">The new engineering proposal evaluates framework data APIs and hydratable rendering while keeping the accepted web/API boundaries. Its current framework-mode build-tool candidate has a recorded beta dependency restriction. The <a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/semantic-preparation-v1-2026-10-05.md">bounded independent review</a> passes the proposal and specific blocker. The later closed private job messages and coordinator acceptance proposal also have <a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/preparation-message-v1-2026-10-05.md">bounded independent review PASS</a>. No production mechanism or dependency is selected; worker authority/isolation, resource and retention rules, the full stable graph and actual runtime evidence remain required.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#semantic-preparation-engineering-proposal">Semantic preparation proposal</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/INTERFACE_CATALOG.md#private-preparation-boundary">Preparation authority boundary</a><a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#private-preparation-message-and-acceptance-proposal">Private build messages and result checks</a></div></details>
<h3>Recommended build sequence after Phase 1 acceptance</h3>
<ol class="flow"><li><strong>Prove the complete first journey</strong>Arrival → reception → first eligible department → information/help → booking, with semantic equivalents.</li><li><strong>Prove movement and loading</strong>Check walls, entrances, crossings, reversals, missing assets, late results, Exit and safe recovery.</li><li><strong>Bring the concept to life</strong>Compare all-around views; refine materials, vegetation, lighting and visitor-enabled sound within measured device budgets.</li><li><strong>Expand with evidence</strong>Review the representative result, then build the remaining wings in their accepted opening order.</li></ol>
<p class="small">This is a researched recommendation, not completed runtime work. The internal inventory accounts for the study's 117 mesh nodes in 15 authoring families; no production chunks were generated. The subsequent <a href="../phase-1-3d/reviews/campus-asset-engineering-v1-2026-10-05.md">independent asset engineering review</a> passes its exact definition and inventory inputs, including source/geometry accounting. Appearance, collision, rights, physical-device budgets and runtime remain unproven. Proposed additional libraries remain candidates. Full Phase 1 acceptance, reviewed production references, detailed budgets and implementation authorization remain required.</p>
<div class="source-links"><a href="../phase-1-3d/CAMPUS_ASSET_BUILD_SPEC.md#researched-engineering-recommendation">Detailed engineering recommendation and primary sources</a><a href="../phase-1-3d/asset-manifest.json">Internal asset inventory</a><a href="04-reconciliation-map.md#engineering-responsibility-and-the-client-brief">How this fits the consolidated definition</a></div>
</section>
<section id="features"><div class="eyebrow">From the system to bounded specifications</div><h2>Four feature drafts carry the same v1 definition.</h2><p>Each specification references the accepted scope and canonical contracts. Security, World and content drafts have bounded independent consistency review. QA review requires a browser-release wording correction; the prepared repair awaits a revision-limit exception. Exact held inputs and founder acceptance remain. None has an executable implementation plan or runtime test result.</p>
<div class="grid two"><article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">DOING · Reviewed draft</span><h3>World and connected campus</h3><p>Explicit entry, four equivalent streams, mouse/touch movement, destinations, reversal-ready loading and optional sound. One coherent campus must support the same approved information and booking as the website.</p><p class="small">Still held: final controls and screens, safe connected geometry, production appearance, rights and measured device budgets.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../../specs/003-3d-experience-completion/spec.md">World specification</a><a href="../../specs/003-3d-experience-completion/checklists/requirements.md">World producer checklist</a><a href="../../specs/003-3d-experience-completion/reviews/world-feature-v1-2026-10-04.md">World definition review and limits</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">DOING · Review correction held</span><h3>Behavior evidence and recovery</h3><p>Verify actual website, API, database, AI, booking, handoff and World behavior. Include denial, failure, concurrency, deletion and restore cases where the feature needs them.</p><p class="small">Review correction held: restore the approved browser release coverage. Exact measurement and recovery inputs, authorized isolated test scope and operational policies remain held. Documentation checks cannot prove application behavior.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../../specs/002-testing-and-monitoring/spec.md">QA specification</a><a href="../../specs/002-testing-and-monitoring/checklists/requirements.md">QA producer checklist</a><a href="../../specs/002-testing-and-monitoring/reviews/qa-feature-v1-2026-10-04.md">Current QA review and finding</a><a href="../../output/research/qa-browser-coverage-repair-2026-10-04.patch">Exact proposed browser correction</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">DOING · Reviewed draft</span><h3>Governed content and semantic SEO</h3><p>Preserve five wings and ten service categories, verified company facts and clearly separated Work/Demos. Initial HTML, metadata, visible facts and all approved release representations must agree.</p><p class="small">Still held: verified copy, content owners/reviewers, rights, legal disclosure and exact publication contracts. A content brief is not a reviewed published page.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../../specs/004-design-services-content/spec.md">Content and SEO specification</a><a href="../../specs/004-design-services-content/checklists/requirements.md">Content producer checklist</a><a href="../../specs/004-design-services-content/reviews/content-feature-v1-2026-10-04.md">Content definition review and limits</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><span class="tag proposed">DOING · Reviewed draft</span><h3>Staff security and privacy</h3><p>Separate staff permissions, protected sessions and controlled emergency access. Check actual denial, consent, private-data routing, expiry, deletion and restore behavior. Administrator access cannot approve its own content or invent private-operation authority.</p><p class="small">Still held: exact identity/session/MFA methods, grants, rate/outage controls and legal/provider mappings, applicable legal/accessibility review and founder acceptance. Mailbox ownership stays undecided.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="../../specs/001-platform-security-hardening/spec.md">Security specification</a><a href="../../specs/001-platform-security-hardening/checklists/requirements.md">Security producer checklist</a><a href="../../specs/001-platform-security-hardening/reviews/security-feature-v1-2026-10-04.md">Security definition review and limits</a></div></article></div>
<details><summary>How will we prove the experience works on real devices?</summary><p>The QA draft proposes recording the actual client, browser, renderer, network/cache conditions and observation method before measurement. Transfer bytes, frame-time distributions, resource ownership and sustained-device behavior need distinct evidence; averages and download size cannot stand in for everything.</p><p>Physical-phone access and exact measurement profiles remain held. Desktop mobile emulation checks layout and selected browser behavior; it cannot prove phone GPU, memory or thermal performance. The discovery of a local desktop is not a selected minimum device, and no performance benchmark has been run.</p><a href="../../specs/002-testing-and-monitoring/spec.md#proposed-device-measurement-method">Proposed measurement method</a></details>
<p class="callout">Dedicated privacy and security aliases are approved. Their ownership remains undecided by founder instruction; channel delivery, restricted access and handling must be verified before operational publication. Definition work continues without assigning an owner.</p>
<p class="small">These later specifications are outside the earlier fifteen-artifact amendment review. Read the <a href="../../specs/README.md">feature index and authority</a> for their precise status. Deployment/provider/cost planning remains deferred.</p></section>
<section id="checkpoint"><div class="eyebrow">Honest checkpoint</div><h2>Accepted scope, reviewed proposals, remaining evidence.</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Review checkpoint table"><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Subject</th><th scope="col">Current authority</th><th scope="col">Still required</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Requirements, brand, UX</th><td>Accepted baselines and later recorded amendments</td><td>Real business/content evidence, final screens and integrated acceptance</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Architecture</th><td>Boundaries accepted D-065; movement/release clarification reviewed</td><td>Detailed data/API/provider and operational contracts</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Movement and nature campus</th><td>Scope/direction and D-071 layout basis accepted; material/sound/storyboard amendments and final-third observations independently reviewed at listed hashes</td><td>Final mechanics, connected floor/collision geometry, coherent model appearance, rights and measured budgets</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Campus engineering</th><td>Research-backed renderer, movement, connected-area loading and landscape recommendations; unchanged study inventoried</td><td>A subsequent bounded independent review passes the asset definition and inventory after the initial credits error. Additional libraries are candidates; appearance, rights, collision, dimensions, final references, measured budgets and runtime proof remain.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Publication, privacy, recovery</th><td>Separate bounded reviews cover release refresh, staff authorization, availability, semantic preparation, private build messages and the browser-resource proposal</td><td>Exact directional schemas, resource origins/style and worker permissions, limits, operational grants, synchronization/provider/identity/retention mechanisms and actual runtime proof; integrated acceptance</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Compatibility</th><td>Retained technology families; bounded metadata, backend-source, lint-recheck, hook-conformance evidence and GSAP-notice reviews cover their exact inputs</td><td>The earlier 61-input review has no verdict. The independently newest frontend set fails strict resolution; its alternative lint chain contains a beta dependency, and the stable native-lint study misses renamed hooks and some custom-Effect/configuration cases, with broader rule coverage incomplete or experimental. No full stable graph is selected. Runtime/platform, licences/provenance, locks and acceptance remain.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Native prototype operation</th><td>Existing user-owned PostgreSQL 17 cluster, API 8001 and web 5173 verified on 4 October; public reads and browser admin sign-in succeeded</td><td>The separate Program Files service remains stopped and port 8000 remains an unrelated WSL relay. Known World hook-order and admin-role defects remain open; this prototype path does not prove free movement, streaming, permissions or production readiness.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Deployment and operating costs</th><td>Deferred by founder D-068; Azure/AWS candidates</td><td>Later provider/region/capacity/cost planning; no selection or spending authorized</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Production application</th><td>Protected prototype evidence</td><td>Complete Phase 1 approval before feature implementation; commits/pushes deferred</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p>Definition review is not runtime certification. Documentation phrase/hash guards and isolated schema checks do not prove application behavior. This board consolidates the discussion and documents; it does not promote the prototype or accept missing production designs.</p>
<p class="small">The <a href="../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/current-definition-amendments-2026-10-04.md">independent amendment review</a> records its exact fifteen input hashes and limits. This page's review-status text was reconciled afterward; its new hash is not substituted into that historical receipt. The underlying proposals and founder decisions are unchanged. Native runtime observations are dated 4 October 2026, not a continuing health guarantee; the static definition viewer is separate from those services. See the <a href="../../README.md#native-local-operation-on-windows">native operating instructions</a>, the <a href="../../output/playwright/native-runtime/runtime-observation.json">nonsecret runtime observation</a> and <a href="../../output/playwright/native-runtime/admin-services.png">verified admin Services view</a>.</p>
